WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.501
-We are so lucky to have

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.634
Fred Armisen back
with us tonight.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.334
Give it up for Fred right
over there.

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:08.767
[ Cheering and applause ]
And, Fred, I'm always

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:09.767
so taken aback.

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:10.868
You have so many projects.

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:13.968
Not just film,
not just television,

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:15.133
not just music,

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.968
but just over a wide breadth
of interests.

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:21.400
And I was just reading in the
trades, as you like to call it,

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.534
that you're launching your first
celebrity fragrance.

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:26.734
-Yes.

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:28.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.033
And, um, it's more like an --
it's like an ink than --

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:33.834
[ Laughter ]
So, it's like

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:36.267
this ink I'm putting out
that's like

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:39.701
it smells like -- it has like
a very pungent, inky smell.

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:42.634
-Okay. Is it actually ink?
Like is it --

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:45.133
If you got it on yourself,
would it stain like ink?

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.067
-It's not about that.
It's about how it smells.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:48.968
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.
-So, it's got

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:51.534
a very sort of like
inky smell to it

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:54.334
and it's called TheFredArmisen.
-Okay.

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:56.601
-And so you just --
-It's called TheFredArmisen?

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:58.300
-Yeah, as one word.
-Okay.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:01.434
-Why did you choose
to make it one word?

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:03.100
-It was my organization.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.234
They choose it for me, so.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:06.701
[ Laughter ]
I have like a whole crew
of people

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:08.601
and they come up with all this
stuff and they are so --

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.200
-They don't even go to you
for approvals?

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.534
-No. They're so talented
and they're so smart.

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:14.767
-Okay.
Do they bully you, Fred?

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.501
It seems like they might
bully you a little.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:17.901
-In their own way,

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:19.467
[ Laughter ]
which is fine. It doesn't --

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:20.467
you know, that's fine with me.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:22.968
But it's a nighttime fragrance.

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:25.734
And, uh, so you just, you know,
like before you go out,

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:26.767
you just put it on.

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:27.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:29.067
-But it doesn't stain like ink?

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:30.701
I want to make sure
because you're doing this

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:32.133
and I feel,
if it stains like ink,

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:33.300
I don't want to put it on.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.767
-It stains like ink,
but it doesn't matter.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:39.000
-It's really --
-It's the smell.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.167
-It's really exciting.

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.033
Give it up for Fred Armisen,
everybody.

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:42.968
[ Cheering and applause ]

